UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Medical Technologies operates three facilities in northern Indiana, headquartered in Warsaw. The company has held ISO 13485:2016 certification since 2003 through SGS United Kingdom Limited, though its founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company provides end-to-end contract manufacturing for orthopedic implants, components, and instrumentation. Its capabilities span design for manufacturability, prototyping, and high-volume production using precision CNC machining, Swiss turning, casting, turning, and finishing. All production is documented through device history records, with in-process inspections, final inspection, and product release audits. Sterile packaging and supply chain management complete the in-house offering.

Precision Medical Technologies serves original equipment manufacturers in orthopedics, including knee, hip, spine, shoulder, trauma and extremities, and minimally invasive surgery markets. Customers rely on the firm for tibial trays, femoral components, patellar components, and partial or total knee implants and instrumentation.

The company emphasizes a 24-hour quote response, vertical integration across its three Indiana sites, and the ability to complete production in a single operation. Its quality system maintains IQ, OQ, and PQ validation, with dimensional accuracy monitored via CMMs, optical comparators, and Keyence measuring systems.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design for manufacturability", "Prototyping", "High-volume production", "Precision CNC machining", "Swiss turn machining", "Casting", "Turning", "Finishing", "Assembly", "Sterile packaging", "Supply chain management", "CMM inspection", "Optical comparator inspection", "Keyence image dimension measurement", "Statistical process control", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation", "Materials expertise", "End-to-end manufacturing"], "industries": ["Orthopedics", "Knee implants and instrumentation", "Hip implants and instrumentation", "Spine implants and instrumentation", "Shoulder implants and instrumentation", "Trauma and extremities", "Minimally invasive surgery (MIS)", "Medical device manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Brown and Sharp Global Image CMM with PC DMIS", "Keyence Image Dimension Measuring System", "Optical comparators (14-inch to 30-inch with video inspection software)", "Thermo Scientific Material Analyzer"], "volume": "Prototype to High Volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24-hour quote response time", "Vertical integration across three Indiana facilities", "ISO 13485:2016 certified since 2003", "Complete production in a single operation", "In-house sterile packaging and supply chain management"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Warsaw, Indiana -> db", "Three facilities in northern Indiana -> /", "ISO 13485:2016 certified since 2003 via SGS UK -> /quality", "End-to-end manufacturing: design, prototype, high-volume, machining, casting, turning, finishing, assembly, sterile packaging, supply chain -> /, /about", "Markets: knee, hip, spine, shoulder, t