UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Molded Plastics operates from Upland, California, where Ted F. VanVoorhis founded the company in 1979 as an ultra‑small‑parts specialty molder serving the electronics and early computer industries. VanVoorhis, a charter member of the Southern California chapter of the Society of Plastics Engineers, quickly established the firm as a leader in what is now known as micromolding. In 2004 his son David assumed leadership and became president and CEO in 2009, continuing the family‑owned operation.

The company specializes in high‑volume runs with a minimum annual program demand of 10,000 units, and supports programs with in‑house 3D printing for rapid prototypes, custom mold design and construction, and a full suite of secondary operations including machining, insert and overmolding, pad printing, hot stamping, thermal transfer decorating, assembly, packaging, and distribution.

Precision serves OEMs and Fortune 500 customers in medical, aerospace, food and beverage, construction, agriculture, irrigation, and electronics sectors. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015.

The company emphasizes a one‑roof model that combines tooling, molding, finishing, and logistics, offers reshoring assistance and mold‑transfer services, and maintains an environmental focus that recycles materials and generates less non‑recyclable waste per week than the average household.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Custom Mold Design and Building", "High-Volume Injection Molding (15\u2013310 ton presses)", "Insert Molding", "Overmolding", "In-Mold Decorating", "Pad Printing", "Hot Stamping", "Thermal Transfer Decorating", "CNC Machining (Secondary Operations)", "Hardware Installation", "Sub-Assembly", "Full Product Assembly", "Packaging and Distribution", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) Analysis", "Mold Flow Analysis", "3D Printing (Prototyping)", "Material and Component Sourcing", "R&D Support", "Quality Management (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Food and Beverage", "Construction", "Agriculture", "Irrigation", "Electronics", "Computer"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (15\u2013310 ton clamping force)", "In-house 3D printer"], "volume": "Minimum 10,000 units annually; high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated: mold building, molding, secondary operations, and assembly under one roof", "Injection molding machines from 15 to 310 tons for small to midsize parts", "Minimum annual program demand of 10,000 units", "In\u2011house 3D printing for rapid prototyping during R&D", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1979 by Ted F. VanVoorhis -> /about", "Family-owned; David VanVoorhis became President/CEO in 2009 -> /about", "Headquartered in Upland, California -> db", "Vertically integrated: mold building, molding, secondary operations, assembly -> /services", "20+ injection molding machines, 15-310 ton clamping pressure, three buildings -> /about, /services", "Minimum annual program demand 10,000 units -> /services", "In-house 3D printing for prototypes -> /services", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality, /about, /services", "Industries served: medical, aerospace, food and beverage, construction, agriculture, irrigation, electronics -> /about, /services, db", "Environmental sustainability: recycling, waste less than average household -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Precision is a vertically integrated, plastic injection molding company that builds custom molds and tooling, manufactures parts and products, and performs a variety of value-added services all under one roof.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "10,000 units annually", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precision-molded-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Plastics, Inc. was founded in 1976 in Beltsville, Maryland, by its current owner with the goal of providing custom plastic fabrication services to a broad range of industries. The company began by supplying merchandise displays and custom store fixtures to large retailers before expanding into more specialized work.

Today the firm operates as a full-service plastics manufacturer offering design, engineering, and manufacturing under one roof. Its capabilities span concept development, industrial design, 3D modeling, prototyping, testing, production planning, material sourcing, and finishing services such as engraving, polishing, and assembly. Fabrications range from one-of-a-kind prototypes to short-run production in plastics, wood, laminate, and metals.

The customer base includes retail chains, the U.S. Navy (for quarter-scale rocket models), national museums requiring complex display cases and archival enclosures, scientific and microscopy facilities needing precision instrument housings, trade-show exhibitors, signage and wayfinding programs, and makers of acrylic furniture and podiums. Projects have included museum-quality cases, laboratory equipment enclosures, trade-show displays, custom podiums, and interior signage systems.

Precision Plastics attributes its differentiation to nearly 50 years of industry experience, deep material expertise, innovative technology such as 3D design and digital fabrication integration, highly skilled craftspeople, rigorous quality control, and project management that keeps jobs on time and on budget.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic fabrication", "Concept development and industrial design", "Engineering analysis and design optimization", "3D design and modeling", "Prototyping and testing", "Production planning and material sourcing", "Short-run manufacturing", "Finishing: engraving, polishing, assembly", "Digital fabrication integration", "Signage fabrication", "Acrylic furniture fabrication", "Museum display case fabrication", "Scientific instrument enclosure fabrication", "Trade show display fabrication", "Project management"], "industries": ["Retail", "Defense (U.S. Navy)", "Museums & Cultural Institutions", "Scientific & Laboratory Equipment", "Trade Shows & Exhibits", "Signage & Wayfinding", "Furniture"], "materials": ["Plastics", "Wood", "Laminate", "Metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to short-run production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nearly 50 years of industry experience", "In-depth material expertise for optimal selection", "3D design and digital fabrication integration", "Highly skilled craftspeople", "Project management to keep projects on time and budget"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 -> db", "Headquarters Beltsville, Maryland -> db", "Founded by current owner -> /about", "Initial work: retail merchandise displays and store fixtures -> /about", "U.S. Navy quarter-scale rocket models -> /about", "Museum display cases and scientific instruments -> /about", "National museums as clients -> /about", "Full-service plastics manufacturing (design, engineering, manufacturing) -> /services", "Prototypes to short-run production -> /services", "Works in plastics, wood, laminate, metals -> /", "Products: museum cases, scientific products, trade show displays, podiums, acrylic furniture, signage -> /services", "Industries: retail, defense, museums, scientific, trade shows, signage, furniture -> /about, /services", "Differentiators: 50 years experience, material expertise, 3D design/digital fabrication, skilled craftspeople, quality control, project management -> /about", "Capabilities: concept development, industrial design, engineering analysis, prototyping, production planning, finishing -> /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Precision Plastics, Inc. is a plastic fabrication company ... we design, engineer and manufacture products in almost any size, design or quantity.", "founded_year": "1976", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precision-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Plastics Packaging Co. (PPPC) was founded in 1963 in Anaheim, California, starting with a simple printing unit.

PPPC manufactures and decorates plastic bottles using injection stretch blow molding, extrusion stretch blow molding, and silk screen printing with multi-head machines. The facility also runs hot-stamping operations. The company produces more than one million containers per day and employs both make-to-order and make-to-stock strategies to align production with demand forecasts.

The company serves cosmeceutical markets with FDA-approved bottles and acts as a certified vendor for that sector. Its customer base ranges from Fortune 500 corporations to small independent businesses, though specific client names are not disclosed.

PPPC attributes its growth to guiding principles of craftsmanship, commitment, quality, technological innovation, and inventiveness maintained over five decades. The firm emphasizes stability, innovation, and customization services as key differentiators that attract and retain customers.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA APPROVED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Stretch Blow Molding", "Extrusion Stretch Blow Molding", "Silk Screen Printing", "Hot-Stamping", "Make to Order", "Make to Stock"], "industries": ["Cosmeceutical"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Injection stretch blow molding machines", "Extrusion stretch blow molding machines", "Multi-head silk screen printing machine", "Hot-stamping equipment"], "volume": "Over 1 million containers per day", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Daily production capacity exceeding 1 million containers", "Dual make-to-order and make-to-stock production strategies", "120,000 sq ft facility with ~150 long-tenured employees", "FDA-approved manufacturing for cosmeceutical bottles", "Multi-head silk screen printing and hot-stamping decoration"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 -> db", "Anaheim, California location -> db", "120,000 sq ft facility -> db", "~150 employees -> db", "Injection stretch blow molding -> db", "Extrusion stretch blow molding -> db", "Silk screen printing with multi-head machines -> db", "Hot-stamping -> db", "Make-to-order and make-to-stock strategies -> db", "Over 1 million containers per day -> db", "FDA APPROVED certification -> db", "Cosmeceutical industry -> /", "Certified vendor for cosmeceutical -> /", "Fortune 500 and small independent customers -> db", "Guiding principles of craftsmanship, commitment, quality, innovation, inventiveness -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We manufacture and decorate more than a million superior quality plastic containers per day.", "founded_year": "1963", "employee_count": "150", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='precision-plastics-packaging-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Precision Wood Finish has operated in Bismarck, North Dakota since 1994. The family-owned business was started by Don and Cindy and grew from a 2,700-square-foot shop serving Bismarck-Mandan into a 7,600-square-foot facility.

The company provides interior and exterior wood staining and finishing services for residential and commercial clients. Its shop-based process uses spray-applied stains, chemical coatings, glazes, and gel stains, with capabilities including custom color matching across wood species, horizontal spraying of doors, and a three-coat topcoat system. The controlled environment limits VOC exposure and ensures consistent results on items such as cabinetry, millwork, stair systems, entry doors, windows, barn doors, and cedar siding.

Customers range from homeowners refinishing kitchen cabinets and fireplace mantels to commercial projects like the NDSU wall art installation and trim packages for local builders. The company also finishes fiberglass and metal entry systems, patio doors, and specialty items such as bar tops.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Spray staining", "Chemical coatings", "Fast-drying finishes", "Penetrating stains", "Specialty applications", "Cabinet finishing", "Glazing", "Gel staining", "Millwork finishing", "Stair system staining", "Interior wood door finishing", "Fiberglass entry system finishing", "Metal entry system finishing", "Patio door finishing", "Window finishing", "Barn door finishing", "Exterior seal and stain", "Custom stain color matching", "Horizontal spray application", "Wax-paper door protection", "VOC-controlled shop environment"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Wood", "Cedar", "Fiberglass", "Metal", "Knotty Alder"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom stain color matching across wood species", "Shop-based finishing for VOC control", "Horizontal spraying of doors with wax-paper protection", "Family-owned since 1994", "7,600 sq ft controlled environment facility"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1994 -> db", "Headquarters Bismarck, North Dakota -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /", "Facility grew from 2,700 to 7,600 sq ft -> /", "Services: interior/exterior wood staining, custom color matching, spray coatings, glazing, gel stain -> /", "Processes: 3 sprayed top coats, 2 heavy sprayed paint coats, horizontal spraying, wax paper protection -> /", "Industries served: residential and commercial -> /", "Example projects: kitchen cabinets, fireplace mantel, NDSU wall art, trim packages, barn doors, cedar siding -> /", "Differentiators: shop-based work for VOC control, custom stain matching, horizontal door spraying -> /", "Owners Don & Cindy mentioned in test