UPDATE companies SET description='Manufacturing was established in 1999 in Mead, Colorado, by Edmond Johnson, who remains president and owner. The company began as a printed circuit board assembly operation and grew organically through word-of-mouth referrals to become one of Colorado''s largest electronics manufacturing service providers, now operating a 45,000-square-foot facility along the Front Range.

The shop runs five manufacturing lines with 125 employees, offering full-service PCB contract manufacturing that spans new product introduction, prototype assembly, surface-mount and through-hole production, box-build integration, and test development. Processes include DEK, Samsung, and Mycronic pick-and-place equipment capable of 01005, BGA, micro-BGA, CGA, and LGA packages; 2D and 3D X-ray inspection; automated optical inspection on every line; selective and dual-wave soldering (RoHS and leaded); automated radial, axial, and DIP insertion; and in-line aqueous cleaning. Engineering partners with over 30 years of PCB experience provide DFM/DFT review, design services, and functional/in-circuit test solutions, while supply-chain management leverages Global Shop Solutions ERP and SiliconExpert''s 250-million-part database for Kanban stocking and obsolescence forecasting.

The program-management approach assigns a technical program manager to each account, and the company emphasizes copy-exact transitions from prototype to volume, dock-to-stock box-build delivery, and turnkey or consigned material models.

Johnson founded the business to deliver quality, on-time products at competitive cost while maintaining a safe, rewarding workplace—a philosophy the company calls its Advantage.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Prototype PCB Assembly", "SMT Production (Surface Mount Technology)", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Box Build Integration (Higher Level Assembly)", "Design Engineering Services", "Functional Test Development", "In-Circuit Test (ICT)", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "2D/3D X-ray Inspection", "Selective Wave Soldering (RoHS and leaded)", "Wave Soldering (lead-free and leaded)", "Automated and Semi-automated Through-Hole Insertion", "Slide-line Technology", "In-line Aqueous Cleaning (DI water closed-loop)", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "Design for Test (DFT)", "Supply Chain Management / Turnkey Procurement", "Kanban Stocking Programs", "Program Management", "BOM Review / SiliconExpert Analysis", "Configuration Change Management", "Copy Exact Processes"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Medical", "Electronics Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Lead-free solder", "Leaded solder", "RoHS-compliant materials"], "equipment": ["DEK pick and place machines", "Samsung SM421 pick and place machine", "Mycronic 200 pick and place machine", "Mycronic SMD Towers", "MyData 100 LXE pick and place machine", "Jewel Box 70T XRAY with Auto BGA Analysis", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI) systems", "Selective wave soldering system", "Lead-free wave soldering systems", "Leaded wave soldering systems", "Automated radial, axial, and DIP insertion machines", "Contact Systems semi-automatic insertion machines", "Slide-line technology", "In-line aqueous cleaning system with DI water closed-loop filtering", "Global Shop Solutions ERP software", "SiliconExpert BOM Manager"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1999 -> db", "Headquarters Mead, 