UPDATE companies SET description='Printwear of Oregon was founded in 1983 in Eugene, Oregon. The company began as a screen printing and embroidery shop serving local businesses and organizations. In 2017, it merged with BirdTracs Embroidery, a well-known apparel logo-wear business, and consolidated operations at a new facility on Highway 99 North.

The shop provides custom screen printing using plastisol, water-based, discharge, and silicone inks, as well as embroidery services. It also sources promotional products such as pens, mugs, magnets, and tote bags. Production takes place at the combined Eugene location, though the company does not disclose facility size or employee count.

Printwear serves a mix of corporate clients, non-profit organizations, musical acts, and event promoters who need branded apparel and merchandise.

