UPDATE companies SET description='RadScan Medical Equipment, Inc. was founded in 1990 in Phoenix, Arizona, by a biomedical engineer who encountered CT scanner downtime caused by contaminants seeping under the cradle into the table interior. With CDC regulations highlighting risks of HIV and hepatitis C exposure during maintenance, he developed a preventive solution: the first CT Slicker® protective cover, which was patented and became the foundation of the company.

Today RadScan develops and manufactures a broad line of medical device accessories, including Slicker® protective covers and cushion table pads for CT, angiography, nuclear medicine, and cardiac catheterization tables. The company operates a 15,000‑square‑foot FDA‑registered and ISO 13485‑certified facility where it performs RF welding and sealing of thermoplastics (polyethylene, polypropylene, PVC, polyurethane, ABS), foam fabrication, industrial sewing, CNC precision cutting, and full product assembly. RadScan reports serving more than 40 countries, 1,600 customers, and offering over 100 imaging products.

The customer base spans original equipment manufacturers, hospitals, clinics, and a global network of dealers and distributors. RadScan partners with OEMs to co‑design new imaging accessories and also sells its branded covers and pads directly to healthcare facilities worldwide.

The company emphasizes its regulatory expertise — maintaining ISO 13485, FDA, EU MDR, RoHS, and REACH compliance — and its American‑made manufacturing as key differentiators. Its design‑to‑production capability allows it to take a concept through regulatory clearance to volume production, a service it promotes to OEMs seeking a single‑source partner.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Contract Manufacturing", "Product Design & Development", "RF Welding & Sealing", "Foam Fabrication", "Industrial Sewing", "Product Assembly", "CNC Precision Cutting"], "industries": ["Medical device accessories", "Diagnostic imaging (CT, angiography, nuclear medicine, cardiac catheterization)", "OEM medical device manufacturing", "Hospitals and clinics", "Medical equipment dealers and distributors"], "materials": ["Polyethylene", "Polypropylene", "Polyvinyl Chloride (PVC)", "Polyurethane", "Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene (ABS)", "Fabrics", "Films", "Foam"], "equipment": ["Large format band saws", "Reciprocating band saws", "Beveling saws", "Industrial sewing equipment", "CNC equipment", "RF welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented Slicker\u00ae contamination barriers for imaging tables", "ISO 13485 and FDA registered U.S. manufacturing facility", "15,000 sq ft of integrated production and warehouse space", "In\u2011house RF welding, foam fabrication, sewing, and CNC cutting", "Design\u2011to\u2011production regulatory support for OEM partners"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1990 by a biomedical engineer -> /about", "Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "ISO 13485 certified, FDA registered, EU MDR, RoHS, REACH compliant -> /", "15,000 sq ft manufacturing and warehouse facility -> /capabilities", "Capabilities: RF welding, foam fabrication, industrial sewing, CNC cutting, product assembly -> /capabilities", "Patented Slicker\u00ae protective covers and cushion table pads -> /", "Serves 40+ countries, 1,600+ customers, 100+ products -> /about", "Customers: OEMs, hospitals, clinics, dealers, distributors worldwide -> /", "Materials: polyethylene, polypropylene, PVC, polyurethane, ABS, fabrics, films, foam -> /capabilities", "Equipment: large format band saws, reciprocating band saws, beveling saws, industrial sewing equipment, CNC equipment -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "develops and manufactures a wide range of high quality products and accessories", "founded_year": "1990", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["FDA registered", "EU MDR compliant", "RoHS compliant", "REACH compliant"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='radscan-medical-equipment-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rapid Packaging is headquartered in Champlin, Minnesota, and was founded in 1988. The company''s lineage traces back to 1943 when Ben Berg established Berg Bag Company in Minneapolis to supply flour sacks to area mills, later expanding into manufacturing lint‑free flour sack towels.

Today Rapid Packaging operates as a packaging solutions distributor and service provider. Its product portfolio spans custom corrugated boxes, FIBC bulk bags, industrial bags (BOPP, polyethylene, woven polypropylene, textile), protective packaging, shrink and stretch films, tapes, and void fill. The firm also supplies end‑of‑line automation equipment — auto baggers, case erectors, case sealers, conveyors, palletizers, shrink wrap systems — and backs them with parts, service, equipment financing, and used‑equipment rentals.

Typical customers include businesses requiring sandbags, FIBCs for bulk handling, and custom corrugated packaging for shipping.

