UPDATE companies SET description='Ready Cable Inc. is headquartered in Fort Worth, Texas, and was founded in 1988 by Robert “Bob” Lemke and his wife, Virginia “Jenny” Lemke. The couple’s roots in concrete go back to 1972, when they started Lemke Concrete in Illinois. After harsh winters prompted a move to Dallas in 1984, they identified a market gap for post‑tension cable materials and services and launched Ready Cable Inc. four years later.

The company manufactures and supplies post‑tension cables, reinforcing steel (rebar) and lumber for concrete reinforcement. Its service side includes estimation and detailing for conventional and post‑tension slabs, jobsite delivery of foundation packages, professional stressing of post‑tension systems, and repair of those systems. The operation serves both residential and commercial projects, from driveway paving to high‑rise foundations.

Customers are primarily concrete contractors and builders in the residential and commercial construction sectors. Ready Cable’s packages have been used on projects ranging from single‑family home slabs to multi‑story commercial towers throughout Texas. The firm also works with its sister company, Nortex Foundation Design, which provides engineered foundation plans when clients lack shop drawings.

The Lemkes started Ready Cable to control the quality and availability of post‑tension materials for their own contracting work, a mission that evolved into a broader commitment to quick turnaround, competitive pricing and reliable field support for other contractors.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Post-tension cable manufacturing", "Rebar supply", "Lumber supply", "Estimation and detailing", "Jobsite delivery", "Post-tension stressing", "Post-tension system repair"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Concrete contracting", "Foundation construction"], "materials": ["Post-tension cables", "Rebar", "Lumber"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Quick turnaround and competitive pricing for concrete contractors", "Multiple Texas locations enabling timely jobsite delivery", "In\u2011house estimation and detailing for conventional and post\u2011tension slabs", "Post\u2011tension stressing and system repair services", "Sister company Nortex Foundation Design supplies engineered foundation plans"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1988 by Robert \"Bob\" Lemke and Virginia \"Jenny\" Lemke -> /about-us", "Origins from Lemke Concrete (1972 Illinois) -> /about-us", "Move to Dallas 1984 -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "Headquarters Fort Worth, Texas -> db (hq_city, hq_state_label)", "Multiple locations across DFW, Houston, Austin, San Antonio -> / (home page)", "Manufactures and supplies post-tension cables, rebar, lumber -> /about-us, / (home page)", "Services: estimation & detailing, jobsite delivery, stressing, post-tension repair -> /services", "Serves residential and commercial construction, concrete contractors -> / (home page)", "Projects from paving to high-rise buildings -> / (home page)", "Sister company Nortex Foundation Design for foundation plans -> /services", "Commitment to quick turnaround, competitive pricing, reliable field support -> / (home page), /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our passion lies in manufacturing and supplying the materials and systems that reinforce the concrete structures around us.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ready-cable-inc-post-tension-rebar-lumber' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Real Tree Woodworking operates from a 3,500-square-foot shop in Duxbury, Vermont, just off Route 100 near Waterbury. The business traces its roots to 2004 when Jon Deerfield founded Nature''s Curve Woodworking in an artist community in Niagara Falls, New York, after earning a BFA in Furniture Design and apprenticing with two master craftsmen—including work on a Frank Lloyd Wright house restoration. Deerfield relocated to Vermont in 2007 to join Wall/Goldfinger, a high-end commercial furniture maker serving clients such as the New York Stock Exchange, the White House, and the Federal Reserve. In spring 2012 he relaunched the venture as Real Tree Woodworking, which has grown steadily since.

The shop produces custom cabinetry, furniture, doors, and architectural trim on a build-to-order basis, and also offers piecework processing of solid wood, sheet goods, real wood veneer, and laminate for other builders and DIYers. A dedicated finishing room rounds out the in-house capabilities. The current team comprises Deerfield and three woodworkers—Matt Joyce (since 2022), John Crowne (since 2021), and D.J. Rummell (since 2025)—working in the 3,500 sq ft facility.

Customers span residential and commercial construction across Vermont and the East Coast (New Hampshire, Massachusetts, New York). The client base includes architects, designers, general contractors, and other woodworking shops. Notable past projects include commercial office furniture for Wall/Goldfinger''s institutional accounts and the Frank Lloyd Wright restoration.

Deerfield emphasizes a "build it well and build it to last" philosophy rooted in his apprenticeship background and the disciplined production standards honed at Wall/Goldfinger, positioning the shop as a reliable partner for both one-off custom pieces and repeat production runs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry", "Furniture making", "Door fabrication", "Architectural trim work", "Piecework/material processing", "Finishing", "Solid wood machining", "Sheet goods processing", "Real wood veneer application", "Laminate fabrication"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Architecture and design", "Furniture manufacturing", "Cabinetry", "Millwork", "Commercial office furniture"], "materials": ["Solid wood", "Sheet goods", "Real wood veneer", "Laminate"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom, build-to-order wood shop", "3,500 sq ft shop with dedicated finishing room", "Over 50 years combined staff experience", "Piecework services for builders and DIYers", "Serves Vermont and East Coast markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 (second life) -> db", "Location Duxbury, Vermont -> db, /", "3,500 sq ft shop at 183 Crossett Hill Road -> /about", "Owner Jon Deerfield, founded 2004 as Nature''s Curve Woodworking -> /about", "Apprenticed with master craftsmen, Frank Lloyd Wright restoration -> /about", "Worked at Wall/Goldfinger 2007-2012, clients NYSE, White House, Federal Reserve -> /about", "Team members: Matt Joyce, John Crowne, D.J. Rummell -> /about", "Products: cabinetry, furniture, doors, architectural trim, piecework -> /", "Capabilities: solid wood, sheet goods, veneer, laminate, finishing -> /about", "Industries: residential, commercial, architects, designers, construction companies, builders, homeowners, DIYers -> /", "Geographic reach: Vermont, NH, MA, NY -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Real T